            "review_title": "Review at Chill Dining - Grill & Seafood Oyster Bar",
            "review_text": "spktravels\nTallman, New York360 contributions\n0\nExcellent throughout but costly\nFeb 2025 • Family\nChill dining restaurant on the 27th floor has an excellent view of district 1. \n\nThe service is very professional and accommodating. It was like we had our own private waitress. Whether this was because for most of our meal my wife and I were the only patrons I don’t know. \n\nFood was excellent and served in the proper order and with proper timing \n\nWe enjoyed French seafood soup, Miyagi oysters, Canadian lobster and fried rice with seafood. Each dish was top quality and extremely tasty. \n\nThe cost for dinner was very high, for Vietnam, but it would have been much more costly in the United States. \n\nIf your budget allows it I highly recommend this restaurant.\nRead more\nWritten February 25, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
